    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23975" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-stinguo</span></b> , stinxi, stinctum, 3,
			v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to instigate</i>, <i>incite</i>, <i>impel</i> (class. only in the <i>part.
				pass.</i>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Christus intus instinxerat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Anim. 26</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">Gell. 17, 20, 7</span></i>, read
			instrinxit).— <i>Part. pass.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">instinctus</span></b> , a, um,
				<i>instigated</i>, <i>incited</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">furore et audaciā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 5, 72, § 188</span></i>
			: his vocibus, <i>fired</i>, <i>animated</i>,
			<i><span class="en">Liv. 9,
				40, 7</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">furiis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 1,
					47</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">injuriā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">divino spiritu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 12, 10, 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">classico,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					2, 11, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in bellum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vell.
					1, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litterarum jucunditatibus instinctae mentes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 9 praef.</span></i>
			</div>
